3. Skia
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
What:     The managed rasterizer and the FreeType text engine port or
          reproduce Skia m88 (as shipped in SkiaSharp 2.88) so that they
          draw exactly what the Skia backend draws: the stroker, dasher,
          contour measure and curve maths (SkStroke, SkStrokerPriv,
          SkDashPath, SkContourMeasure, SkGeometry); path builders; the
          hairline and supersampling scan converters and edge builders;
          mask, image and rect blurs and nine-patch shadows; N32 blend
          arithmetic and A8 mask blits; gradients; unpremultiply; and the
          text mask gamma (SkMaskGamma).
Where:    bibui-raster-managed/ (Bibui.Raster.Managed,
          Bibui.Raster.Managed.Backend) and bibui-text-freetype/
          (Bibui.Text.FreeType). Each type that does so names the Skia
          source it follows.
Licence:  BSD 3-Clause.
          Copyright (c) 2011 Google Inc. All rights reserved.
Source:   https://skia.org

